# Luminita, horse-tender of the Tser Pool camp (docs/voice/luminita.md). Her brother Nicu is the hanged man at the
# crossroads (crossroads.dialogue). The party can tell her (quest the_hanged_vistana `told`), give her his earring,
# or never say. She knows why he was hanged, and it is her fault.

~ start
if flag.nicu_kin_told
-> after_news
endif
if flag.luminita_met
-> again
endif
set luminita_met
Narrator: A young woman with a horse brush in her fist looks up from the pen, sees that you are not who she hoped, and goes back to brushing harder than the horse needs.
Luminita: You came along the road. Did you pass a rider? Black hair, silver earring, a laugh you can hear across a field. Too handsome, and he knows it.
if not flag.crossroads_gallows_seen
quest the_hanged_vistana asked
endif
-> menu

~ again
Luminita: Still no rider on the road? No. You'd have said.
-> menu

~ menu
* [if flag.crossroads_gallows_seen] We found a Vistana at the crossroads. Hanged. -> tell
* [if not flag.crossroads_gallows_seen] We passed no one. -> none
* Who is he? -> who
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Help her with the horse. -> horse_ok | horse_fail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ none
Luminita: Then he's still in Vallaki, drinking the money. Good. I hope he drinks all of it and comes home with a headache.
-> END

~ who
Luminita: Nicu. My brother. He rode to Vallaki four days ago to sell a mare, and said he'd be back the next night with a sack of flour and a new song. He always comes back with a new song.
-> menu

~ horse_ok
Narrator: The grey gelding stops sidling and leans its whole weight on you, the way horses do when they've decided you are furniture.
Luminita: Huh. He doesn't do that for anyone but Nicu. Fine. You can stay.
attitude luminita friendly
-> menu

~ horse_fail
Narrator: The gelding steps squarely on a boot. Luminita does not hide her smile very well.
Luminita: He doesn't like strangers. Neither do I. It's nothing personal; we just have taste.
-> menu

~ tell
Narrator: The brush stops.
Luminita: Hanged. For what?
Narrator: You tell her about the board round his neck, and the two words written on it.
Luminita [angry]: He was no thief.
Luminita [sad]: The mare was mine. I found her loose in the woods with a Vallaki brand on her rump and a broken halter, and I said, sell her, Nicu, sell her back to them, nobody will know. I said nobody will know.
set luminita_confessed
interject tag:loyal: You couldn't have known what they'd do.
interject class:cleric: A rope is the hangman's sin, child. Not yours.
-> told

~ told
set nicu_kin_told
quest the_hanged_vistana told
attitude luminita friendly
attitude stanimir friendly
if flag.nicu_cut_down
Luminita: You cut him down. Strangers, and you cut him down and put him in the ground.
Narrator: She goes into the wagon behind her and comes back with a small corked bottle, which she pushes into the nearest hand without looking at whose it is.
give potion_of_healing
Luminita: Grandmother's remedy. It tastes like plums and regret. Take it, before I change my mind.
elif flag.crossroads_dead_cleared
Luminita: And he got up again, and you put him down. Good. Good. He'd have hated walking around for somebody else.
else
Luminita [angry]: And you left him hanging there. For the crows. Go away. I'll ride out to him myself.
endif
-> told_menu

~ told_menu
* [if flag.nicu_token_taken] Give her his earring. -> earring
* Leave her be. -> END

~ earring
Narrator: She takes the silver horse's head, looks at it for a long time, and puts it in her own ear without a word.
Luminita: There. Now he's still riding.
approve wren_featherfoot +1 liriel_dawnsong +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You gave Luminita the earring of the brother she lost
-> END

~ after_news
if not flag.luminita_met
set luminita_met
Narrator: A young woman in the horse pen looks up, and you know before she speaks that Stanimir has told her.
Luminita [sad]: You're the ones who found Nicu. Stanimir told me. I don't want to talk about it. Ask me something else.
elif flag.nicu_cut_down
Luminita: You again. The ones who cut him down. Sit with the horses if you like. They're better company than people.
else
Luminita: You again. I'm still brushing the same horse. It's very clean now.
endif
* Ask about Vallaki. -> vallaki
* Ask about the Vistani by the lake. -> lake_camp
* Goodbye. -> END

~ vallaki
Luminita: Walls, bells, banners, and a burgomaster who throws a festival every week and calls you a traitor if you don't smile at it. They hanged my brother for a horse. Smile at the gate.
-> after_news

~ lake_camp
Luminita: Our cousins camp by the lake outside Vallaki. Arrigal runs it. He smiles more than I do and means it less. Tell him Luminita says the horse was mine. Watch his face.
-> after_news
